 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? For adults, yes. Children under ten are often fine, especially with parents right by them. Layers help. A thin base layer that wicks sweat, plus a thin glove that stops the cold from touching your fingers. The bus is usually fine, even with the occasional snowflake. Stay away from puddles and don't cross cold water. yes. Proper winter tyres or tyres with the mountain snowflake symbols make a huge difference. They' designed to grip ice and snow much better than tyres alone.",
